# F9, DEV-50: a call-group Remove the 30 s TTL voids while its leaf is still present is re-driven by
# the instance with the same action, so the call stays frozen and the member is still removed by the
# next commit. A void alone would lift the freeze and leave carol decrypting the call.
instance dilla
client alice
client bob
client carol
group call kind=call target=e3e3e3e3e3e3e3e3e3e3e3e3e3e3e3e3 community=none creator=alice
join bob call via=external
sync alice
join carol call via=external
sync alice
sync bob
kick alice carol
expect_425 send alice call before the removal is committed
advance_clock 31s
expect_425 send alice call the re-driven remove still holds the call
commit alice call
sync bob
expect_reject E_LEAF_NOT_CURRENT send carol call am I still in the call
send alice call carol is out
expect_decrypts bob call carol is out
